# 07 - Combination Lock

## Objective

Create a program using an ESP32 where you have to press the correct sequence of a password using buttons and 2 LEDs for visual feedback.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 2 LEDs
- 2 220 Ω resistors
- 3 Push buttons
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- INPUT_PULLUP
- digitalWrite()
- Debouncing Mechanics
- if statements
- variables

## Wiring

- LED1 Anode → GPIO 21 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED1 Cathode → GND 
- LED2 Anode → GPIO 23 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED2 Cathode → GND 
- Push button pin 1 → GPIO 22
- Push button pin 2 → GND

## Expected Result

When the user enters the correct sequence, LED1 lights up. If the user enters an incorrect sequence, LED2 lights up.

## What I Learned

- How to use millis() correctly 
- Timing without delay()
- States

